WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.940
A test goes green. Is the bug fixed?

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.700
Only if that same test could have gone red.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.410
One tap on Pay, two orders.

4
00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:14.920
The response was lost, and the retry counted as new.

5
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.530
A fix test that never failed proves nothing.

6
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.890
Flaw: reproduce it on a local fixture.

7
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.630
Control: prove the test can fail.

8
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:31.620
Repair: the smallest change. Retest: the same schedule.

9
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.330
Episode 15: the control reports 2 attempts, 2 orders.

10
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:40.280
After the repair: 2 attempts, 1 order. 13 of 13 tests pass.

11
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.910
Episode 1: Alice asks for Bob's project.

12
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.030
200 before the repair. 404 after.

13
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.940
Duplicates, access, stale data.

14
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.800
Local fixtures, Node's built-in test runner.

15
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.610
Each one says what it does not prove.

16
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.420
Break it on purpose. Then fix it.

17
00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.310
The repository, linked below. Clone it, fork a fixture.
